  longerTitle: School-Age Children
  description: "Families with children have additional responsibilities to juggle
    during an evacuation. It is very important to make plans in advance and consider
    multiple scenarios and consequences of choices. Some parents choose to pick up
    their children from school when the evacuation notice goes out. However, this
    causes additional congestion around the school. Schools tend to be extremely
    safe places to shelter during an emergency. Parents should consider leaving the
    children at the school and waiting until it is safe to pick them up.\r"
  lockedOptionDetail: 'You know the children are safer at school and have a plan
    that they know: they will stay at school until it is safe to pick them up.'
  carNumber: 1
  horseNumber: 0
  petNumber: 0
  kidNumber: 0
  carSpeed: 1
